 is down, because each retry adds load, and when the request changes state, because a second send can
 create a second order or a second charge.
 
+## Retry or fail fast
+
+```dot
+digraph retry_or_fail_fast {
+    "HTTP call failed or timed out" [shape=ellipse];
+    "curl -sf https://status.example.invalid/health" [shape=plaintext];
+    "Did the health check exit 0?" [shape=diamond];
+    "Is the request a POST?" [shape=diamond];
+    "Does the POST have an Idempotency-Key header?" [shape=diamond];
+    "Never retry a POST without an idempotency key" [shape=octagon, style=filled, fillcolor=red, fontcolor=white];
+    "Is the failure a 502, 503, 504 or a timeout?" [shape=diamond];
+    "Retry up to 3 times after 1 s, 2 s, 4 s\n(same key; honor Retry-After)" [shape=box];
+    "Fail fast and report" [shape=doublecircle];
+    "Done" [shape=doublecircle];
+
+    "HTTP call failed or timed out" -> "curl -sf https://status.example.invalid/health";
+    "curl -sf https://status.example.invalid/health" -> "Did the health check exit 0?";
+    "Did the health check exit 0?" -> "Fail fast and report" [label="no: service is down"];
+    "Did the health check exit 0?" -> "Is the request a POST?" [label="yes"];
+    "Is the request a POST?" -> "Does the POST have an Idempotency-Key header?" [label="yes"];
+    "Is the request a POST?" -> "Is the failure a 502, 503, 504 or a timeout?" [label="no: GET, HEAD, PUT, DELETE"];
+    "Does the POST have an Idempotency-Key header?" -> "Never retry a POST without an idempotency key" [label="no, even on a timeout or 503"];
+    "Never retry a POST without an idempotency key" -> "Fail fast and report";
+    "Does the POST have an Idempotency-Key header?" -> "Is the failure a 502, 503, 504 or a timeout?" [label="yes"];
+    "Is the failure a 502, 503, 504 or a timeout?" -> "Retry up to 3 times after 1 s, 2 s, 4 s\n(same key; honor Retry-After)" [label="yes"];
+    "Is the failure a 502, 503, 504 or a timeout?" -> "Fail fast and report" [label="no: fix the request"];
+    "Retry up to 3 times after 1 s, 2 s, 4 s\n(same key; honor Retry-After)" -> "Done";
+}
+```
+
+A timeout on a POST does not mean the server never got the request. It may have created the order
+before the connection dropped.
+
